      "summary": "Version : v1.3.2",
      "content": "# Beacon v1.3.2 Real Project Validation\n\n**Version**: `v1.3.2`  \n**Status**: `validated in isolated real-project workflow`  \n**Validated project**: `/Users/apple/Developer/Personal/products/shopxo_canada`  \n**Validation worktree**: `/tmp/shopxo-canada-beacon-branch-s3mWLX`  \n**Validated docs line**: `v1.0.0`  \n**Validated feature**: `admin-merchandising-analytics`  \n**Date**: `2026-04-15`\n\n## Goal\n\nUse a real development project to prove Beacon `v1.3.2` public human-facing surfaces are stable enough for release:\n\n- `help`\n- `status`\n- `implement`\n- `qa`\n- `release`\n\nThe validation must prove that current-feature closure can converge through:\n\n- isolated context repair\n- frozen requirement materials\n- technical review contract\n- `implement` team / Ralph surfaces\n- browser-capable QA/session/profile execution\n- `release scorecard`\n\n## Safety Model\n\n- Main project worktree was treated as user-owned and dirty.\n- Read-only validation was performed on the real repo first.\n- All write-path and browser-runtime validation was executed only in isolated copies/worktrees.\n- No write-path validation was performed on the user's main working tree.\n\n## What Was Validated\n\n### 1. Context / Runtime / Delegation\n\n- `doctor setup-context`\n- `doctor verify-context`\n- `doctor verify-subagent-runtime`\n- `doctor verify-subagent-delegation`\n\nResult:\n\n- context inheritance and `global-boundaries` checks passed\n- Codex / Claude skill roots were detected\n- delegation readiness passed after implementation-plan / workflow artifacts were materialized\n\n### 2. Implement Team / Ralph\n\n- `implement plan`\n- `implement run --mode team --runner codex-subagents --host-runtime codex --dry-run`\n- `implement run --mode team --runner gstack --host-runtime claude --dry-run`\n- `implement run --mode ralph --runner codex-subagents --host-runtime codex --dry-run`\n- `implement run --mode ralph --runner gstack --host-runtime claude --dry-run`\n- `implement ralph-status`\n\nResult:\n\n- `team` path was validated on both Codex-native and Claude handoff surfaces\n- `ralph` state persisted and exposed next-step state\n- stale Ralph blocker precedence in `help` was corrected after current-feature QA became release-ready\n\n### 3. Browser QA / Session / Profile\n\n- formal QA bundle for `admin-merchandising-analytics` was rewritten to browser-capable smoke / functional / compatibility layers\n- `qa session save`\n- `qa session use`\n- feature-bound `beacon.config.yaml` profile\n- local `evis-admin` dev server startup\n- `qa team-run`\n- direct `auto-test create qa9` browser validation\n\nResult:\n\n- browser-capable layers were selected from the formal QA matrix\n- `agent-browser` executed against real `/login` page flow\n- browser task / browser evidence artifacts were generated\n- at least one browser case passed\n- final isolated run reached feature-level `release_ready=true`\n\n## Beacon Defects Found And Fixed During Validation\n\n### 1. `qa run --help` hid real feature-aware options\n\nFix:\n\n- public `qa run` help surface was updated to show real feature / project / version / json options\n\n### 2. Browser runner artifact writeback broke on `/tmp` vs `/private/tmp`\n\nFix:\n\n- browser runner common path handling now tolerates macOS path aliases\n\n### 3. `qa team-run` returned non-zero even when final feature-aware QA status was `passed`\n\nFix:\n\n- feature-aware QA exit code now normalizes to `0` when final status is `passed`\n\n### 4. `help` preferred stale Ralph blocker over current authoritative feature scorecard\n\nFix:\n\n- current-feature `ready_for_release` state now overrides stale Ralph repair signals in `help`\n\n### 5. `release scorecard` / `status --board` missed authoritative feature scorecard closure\n\nFix:\n\n- release aggregation now accepts authoritative feature scorecard closure for modern Beacon lines\n- project profile gate fallback from feature scorecard is supported\n- status semantics were clarified between current-feature closure and version-line package closure\n\n## Final Validated State\n\nFor the isolated real-project worktree:\n\n- `help` returns `blocked=false`\n- `help.next_step.action = release-check`\n- `qa team-run` completes through browser-capable QA/session/profile flow\n- `release scorecard.release_ready = true`\n- `status --board` shows `release.ready: True`\n\nImportant semantic note:\n\n- `release.ready` now correctly reflects current-feature closure readiness\n- version-line package closure remains a separate governance surface and may still be open without invalidating current-feature release readiness\n\n## Release Recommendation\n\n`v1.3.2` is ready to use `beacon-real-project-validation` as a release gate for real-project acceptance.\n\nRecommended release rule:\n\n1. local Codex / Claude Beacon skill install must point to the current `skills/beacon/` package\n2. `beacon-real-project-validation` must pass on at least one isolated real project\n3. current-feature closure readiness must be proven through `help`, `qa`, `release scorecard`, and `status`\n4. any remaining version-line closure gaps must be explicitly documented rather than silently ignored\n",
